@* One poster card for the grid view: the cover art is the hero, with a title and optional meta captioned underneath.
   Shared by the inventory list pages, Wishlist and Watch Next, so the markup and its model (a stretched link opens the detail, actions sit above it by z-index) exist once. *@

<div class="kt-grid-card">
    @* Without an Href (a read-only shared card the recipient can't open) there is no stretched link,
       so the card isn't a dead link and its action overlay stays the only clickable thing. *@
    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Href))
    {
        @* rel is set only with target, since it matters only on a new-tab link and every in-app card navigates in the same tab. *@
        <a class="stretched-link" href="@Href" target="@Target" rel="@(Target == "_blank" ? "noopener noreferrer" : null)"
           aria-label="@(LinkLabel ?? Title)"></a>
    }
    <div class="kt-grid-cover @Shape">
        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(ImageUrl))
        {
            <img src="@ImageUrl" alt="" loading="lazy"/>
        }
        else
        {
            <CoverPlaceholder Title="@Title"/>
        }
    </div>
    @* Actions (delete) are a direct child of the card, not inside .kt-grid-cover.
       The cover's hover transform creates a stacking context, which would trap the button's z-index below the card's stretched link and make it unclickable.
       As a sibling of the link, its z-index wins. *@
    @Actions
    <div class="kt-grid-caption">
        <div class="kt-grid-title">@Title</div>
        @if (MetaContent is not null)
        {
            <div class="kt-grid-meta">@MetaContent</div>
        }
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Detail-page URL the whole card links to.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Href { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Anchor target for <see cref="Href"/>.
    /// Unset (same tab) for the in-app detail pages every inventory list opens.
    /// "_blank" for a card that leaves the app, like an Explore suggestion opening its provider page, so reading up on a title doesn't lose the list being worked through.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Target { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Accessible name of the card link when the destination isn't simply "the item" ("Titanic on IMDb").</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? LinkLabel { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? Title { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? ImageUrl { get; set; }

    /// <summary>See <see cref="ItemThumb.Shape"/>: unset for portrait, "square" (albums), "wide" (games).</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Shape { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// The caption's second line (year and creator text, flag pills, badges).
    /// Named to avoid the HTML &lt;meta&gt; element.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? MetaContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Optional overlays on the cover (a delete button), raised above the stretched link by z-index.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Actions { get; set; }
}
